 yeah the andrew luck  thing threw a curveball but  at the same time i think you're right  mike i mean the colts  you know like opposite of like the  raiders  i think there's there's a few things to  talk about on their team where you just  go  man that's that's pretty special what  they got there you know first off  they're offensive line  it's special yes i mean carson wentz we  know what he can do when healthy and  things like that  you know the skill position guys pretty  good running get running backs  good i mean defensive line pretty damn  special and now you got a quiddie pay to  come off the edges  really the only issue on their team was  like lack of edge  threat and quitty pay and even their  their second pick  uh odingbo from vanderbilt are  are both edge rushing type of football  players so  they're really rounding out the roster  right mike and i just look at them i'm  with you i look at it and just go  wait this team is really good they're  like  edge super bowl window type of football  team  and now does carson wentz you know with  acquitty pay  kind of put them over the edge to where  we start off early in 2021 going no like  we thought the colts were on the edge of  the super bowl window they're in the  window like they're that kind of team  and i have a feeling we could be saying  that about them you know four or five  weeks into the year  and it is amazing to think how  differently we feel about the cults if  they had  beaten the bills and they did give the  bills everything they could handle and i  wonder whether or not philip rivers  would have stayed around for one more  year i mean there's an alternate history  gurgling around out there involving the  colts but they may be better off long  term  with carson wentz if wentz becomes  again the guy that he was the guy that  he was when frank reich was in  philadelphia  the guy that frank wright believes he  can be that's really the key to this  team  this gamble they've made on carson wentz  the 